---
import { SEQ_LEN, TOKENS } from "../lib/transformer/constants";
import figure1 from "../assets/images/transformer.png";

// Static on purpose. The hero is the first thing on a phone over a bad
// connection, and none of it needs JavaScript: the equation is markup, the
// sentence comes from the same constant every chapter reads, and the formula
// classes are shared with the interactive version in chapter 5 so the two can't
// drift apart typographically.
//
// The paper's own Figure 1 sits beside the equation as an orientation cue: the
// equation is the mechanism, the diagram is where it lives. It is reproduced with
// credit — arXiv:1706.03762 is under arXiv's perpetual non-exclusive licence,
// which is not a Creative Commons grant, so this is a fair-dealing reproduction
// for study and review rather than a licensed one. Chapter 10's architecture
// diagram remains original work and is not traced from this; see CLAUDE.md.
//
// A plain `<img>` on the imported asset rather than Astro's `<Image>`: the
// optimising component needs `sharp`, and adding a native binary two days from a
// deadline risks the CI install, which runs `--frozen-lockfile` on Linux under a
// pnpm config that only allows builds for esbuild. So the original PNG ships as-is
// at 159KB. Width and height come from the import metadata so the space is
// reserved before it loads and nothing shifts.
---

<header class="hero">
  <p class="hero__eyebrow num">Vaswani et al., 2017</p>

  <h1 class="hero__title">Attention Is All You Need</h1>

  <p class="hero__standfirst">
    The paper that replaced recurrence with a single operation: score every pair
    of words, turn the scores into weights, and mix. Everything below is that
    operation, run on one six-word sentence with numbers small enough to check by
    hand.
  </p>

  <div class="hero__pair">
    <div>
      <div class="hero__formula formula" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="formula__fn math">softmax</span>
        <span class="formula__paren math">(</span>
        <span class="formula__fraction">
          <span class="formula__numerator">
            <span class="math formula__glyph">QK<sup>T</sup></span>
          </span>
          <span class="formula__denominator math">
            <math class="sqrt" display="inline">
              <msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt>
            </math>
          </span>
        </span>
        <span class="formula__paren math">)</span>
        <span class="formula__v math">V</span>
      </div>
      <p class="sr-only">
        The equation: softmax of Q times K transpose, divided by the square root
        of d sub k, times V.
      </p>
      <p class="hero__caption">The mechanism, in one line.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="hero__figure">
      <img
        src={figure1.src}
        width={figure1.width}
        height={figure1.height}
        alt="Figure 1 of the paper: two stacked columns. On the left the encoder — input embedding, plus positional encoding, then multi-head attention and a feed-forward network, each followed by Add and Norm, repeated N times. On the right the decoder — the same shape but with masked multi-head attention first, then a second attention block taking its keys and values from the encoder, ending in a linear layer and a softmax to output probabilities."
        decoding="async"
        class="hero__figure-img"
      />
      <figcaption class="hero__figure-caption">
        Figure&nbsp;1 from <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.03762">Vaswani et al.,
        “Attention Is All You Need” (arXiv:1706.03762)</a>, reproduced for study and
        review. Chapter&nbsp;10 redraws this architecture from the page's own
        constants.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <ol class="hero__sentence" aria-label={`The worked example, ${SEQ_LEN} tokens`}>
    {
      TOKENS.map((token, i) => (
        <li class="token" data-token={token} data-position={i}>
          <span class="token__word">{token}</span>
          <span class="token__index num">{i}</span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <p class="hero__note">
    Two of those six tokens are the same word. Chapter&nbsp;3 is about why that is
    a problem, and what the paper does about it.
  </p>
</header>
